    <GaugingStation location="The Forge Brecon" name="Honddu" number="56003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Three-bay compound crump weir. Station discontinued 1984.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Weir centre crest width is 2.438m, flanking crests are 4.877m. Steep high banks on each flank. Good fall in river bed d/s ensures modularity at all stages. Current meter gaugings were taken to confirm theoretical rating.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Three-bay compound crump weir built in 1963 replacing problematic river section that was affected by bed scour and siltation of intake pipe and closed in 1960. Station discontinued 1984.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Upland catchment, predominantly impermeable geology of Old Red Sandstone with an inlier of the Ludlow Series. Mainly rough grassland and moorland.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Not gauged to within 30% of QMED. However, theoretical rating is expected to perform well up to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating beyond QMED cannot be validated." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
